<Layouts.app flash={@flash}>
  <span class="ok">Server running</span>
  <h1>PakChat server</h1>
  <p>
    This is the relay. It holds a message only until the other phone picks it up,
    then deletes it. The chats themselves live on the phone, not here.
  </p>

  <h2>What is wired up so far</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Phoenix is serving this page.</li>
    <li>Postgres is connected (the page would not load if it were not).</li>
    <li><code>/api/health</code> answers with JSON, for the host to check later.</li>
    <li><code>/dev/dashboard</code> shows live memory, processes and requests.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Next</h2>
  <p>
    Phase 1 is the encryption spike, then phase 2 turns this into the real relay:
    accounts, devices, channels and the waiting-message table.
  </p>
</Layouts.app>
